        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(lmstudio): set supportsTools only for native tool-trained models",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nLM Studio discovery already reads `capabilities.trained_for_tool_use`, but catalog `compat` never set `supportsTools`. Native-trained models therefore relied only on core’s permissive default, with no explicit catalog signal when LM Studio reports native tool training.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nClawSweeper re-review (and LM Studio’s documented tools contract) showed that `trained_for_tool_use: false` means “untrained / less reliable default tool mode”, not “tools unsupported”. Mapping false → `compat.supportsTools: false` would silently strip tools from existing users.\n\nThis revision only maps `trained_for_tool_use: true` → `compat.supportsTools: true`. False and omitted stay unset so OpenClaw keeps the permissive default (`supportsTools !== false`) and LM Studio’s default tool-use path remains available. Native quality still surfaces via the existing `trainedForToolUse` / `tool-use` tag path.\n\nAI-assisted: yes. I inspected the LM Studio wire mapper, discovery spread into catalog compat, sibling Venice/Ollama `supportsTools` semantics, and LM Studio’s OpenAI-compat tools docs before the change.\n\n## User Impact\n\nModels LM Studio marks as natively trained for tools get an explicit `supportsTools: true` catalog flag. Models that report `false` or omit the field keep tools enabled (no capability regression on upgrade).\n\n## Evidence\n\n| Layer | Proof | Result |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| L1 | `mapLmstudioWireEntry`: true → `supportsTools: true`; false → unset; omitted → unset | pass |\n| L2 | `discoverLmstudioModels` still spreads `base.compat` (tools only when true) + `supportsUsageInStreaming` | pass |\n| Rank-up | Removed false→`supportsTools: false` per ClawSweeper recommended option | done |\n| Gate | `oxfmt` + `oxlint` + focused vitest | pass |\n\n```text\npnpm exec oxfmt --check extensions/lmstudio/src/models.ts extensions/lmstudio/src/models.test.ts\npnpm exec oxlint extensions/lmstudio/src/models.ts extensions/lmstudio/src/models.test.ts\npnpm exec vitest run extensions/lmstudio/src/models.test.ts -t \"trained_for_tool_use|maps trained\"\n→ 1 passed (26 skipped)\n```\n\nHead: `5e1d39e7089ba02fa13c29a280560b6eac26dcfb` (on `d2ca8162e7b0ee7837d731512e670927c7af1e92`)\n\n```text\nextensions/lmstudio/src/models.ts       +28 -1\nextensions/lmstudio/src/models.test.ts  +29 -0\n```\n\nUpstream contract note: LM Studio documents that all models support at least some tool use; `trained_for_tool_use` distinguishes native training from default prompt/format fallback ([LM Studio tools docs](https://lmstudio.ai/docs/developer/openai-compat/tools)).\n",
        "branch": "fix/lmstudio-trained-tool-use-supports-tools",
